      "content": "The thing is, the board is actually pretty concerned about the quality gap. One of the senior editors mentioned that moving to a tool that only checks citations and formatting might cause us to miss the deeper, conceptual flaws in the papers—the stuff you usually catch. They're worried that by gaining transparency, we're actually losing the ability to maintain the journal's high impact factor. I'm just the editor, so I'm following orders, but it's definitely a tough trade-off.",
